==English==

===Etymology===
From French ''[[escapade#French|escapade]]'', "the act of escaping" or "a trick" < Old Spanish ''[[escapada]]'' < Old Spanish ''[[escapar]]'' < Vulgar Latin {{term|excappare|excappāre|lang=la|to escape}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|ĕs'kə-pād'}}
* {{rhymes|eɪd}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[daring]] or [[adventurous]] act; an undertaking which goes against [[convention]].

